Compa retains PicoClaw's agent loop, tool registry, skills, sessions, model
providers, gateway, and web cockpit, and adds a detached-module protocol
(pkg/modproto, internal/module) under which capabilities are supplied by
separate local processes rather than linked into the binary.

The product has been rebranded throughout: module path, executable names,
configuration and environment variables, and user-facing strings are Compa's
own.

Compa is not affiliated with or endorsed by Sipeed or the PicoClaw project.
"PicoClaw" is named here solely to give the attribution the MIT License
requires.
